# Day 02 – Time Limit Exceeded & Time Complexity of Python Operations

## 1. Time Limit Exceeded (TLE) Error

### What is Time Limit Exceeded?

Time Limit Exceeded (TLE) is an error that occurs when an algorithm takes more time to execute than the maximum time allowed by the platform.

In coding platforms, every problem may have a time limit, such as 1 second, 2 seconds, etc.

If our program exceeds the given time limit, the platform displays a **Time Limit Exceeded (TLE)** error.

### Understanding the 1-Second Rule

As a rough estimation:

- 1 second ≈ 10⁸ (100 million) simple operations.

This is only an approximate guideline. Actual execution time depends on the programming language, hardware, operation type, and platform.

### What Are Constraints?

Constraints define the limits of the input given in a problem.

For example:

```text
1 <= n <= 100000
```

This means the value of n can range from 1 to 100000.

Constraints help us determine which algorithm and time complexity are suitable for solving a problem.

### Important Points

- Always check the time limit before solving a problem.
- Understand the input constraints.
- Choose an efficient algorithm.
- An algorithm that works for small inputs may fail for large inputs.
- Higher time complexity can lead to TLE for large inputs.

